      "notes": "All claims are well-grounded in cited evidence. The source_support check is satisfied: the JRF/CPP figures (E17, E32) are correctly labelled 'projected' and the rationale correctly flags their advocacy orientation and absence of OBR/IFS verification. The IFS scepticism (E11) is incorporated appropriately rather than suppressed. Tier integrity is clean \u2014 no projected figure is presented as measurable. Magnitude/timing are justified: gross costs in the \u00a31bn+ range but characterised as 'minor' relative to total public spending, which is defensible. The 'worsens' direction is supported by the unfunded-spending logic with no committed offset, and the rationale does not false-balance \u2014 it acknowledges offsetting is plausible but unverified, correctly declining to flip to 'mixed'. No party-blind issues; no motive attribution. The claim about 'doubling representing a near-doubling of the flat-rate bill' (E1) is a reasonable arithmetic inference from the baseline rate, not an overstatement. One minor note: E17 and E32 model a slightly different scheme (6 weeks at 90% AWE) than the proposed one-month at 90%, so the figures are analogous rather than directly applicable \u2014 the rationale acknowledges this implicitly ('comparable scheme') which is sufficient but could be made more explicit. Not a blocking issue."
    },
